From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sachintu47 <sachintu47@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Sep 2024 06:50:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Make SQLite database compression use DEFAULT_COMPRESSION

Change SQLite database compression from hardcoded CR_CW_BZ2_COMPRESSION
to use the configurable CR_DEFAULT_COMPRESSION macro, providing
consistency with XML metadata compression.

This allows SQLite databases (primary.sqlite, filelists.sqlite,
other.sqlite) to respect the DEFAULT_COMPRESSION_METHOD CMake option,
including the no-compression option added for z/OS.

Benefits for z/OS:
- Consistent compression behavior for all repository metadata
- Faster repository generation when using no-compression
- Lower CPU usage during repository creation
- Flexibility to choose compression based on workload needs

Note: dnf5 uses libsolv's solv_xfopen() which transparently handles
decompression of .sqlite.bz2, .sqlite.gz, .sqlite.zst, and uncompressed
.sqlite files based on file extension, so clients will work regardless
of compression method chosen.

Signed-off-by: sachintu47 <sachintu47@gmail.com>
---
 src/createrepo_c.c | 2 +-
 src/mergerepo_c.h  | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/createrepo_c.c b/src/createrepo_c.c
index 197d78e..4bb1bbe 100644
--- a/src/createrepo_c.c
+++ b/src/createrepo_c.c
@@ -828,7 +828,7 @@ main(int argc, char **argv)
     const char *sqlite_compression_suffix = NULL;
     const char *compression_suffix = NULL;
     cr_CompressionType xml_compression = CR_DEFAULT_COMPRESSION;
-    cr_CompressionType sqlite_compression = CR_CW_BZ2_COMPRESSION;
+    cr_CompressionType sqlite_compression = CR_DEFAULT_COMPRESSION;
     cr_CompressionType compression = CR_DEFAULT_COMPRESSION;
 
     if (cmd_options->compatibility) {
diff --git a/src/mergerepo_c.h b/src/mergerepo_c.h
index 96fc147..763e076 100644
--- a/src/mergerepo_c.h
+++ b/src/mergerepo_c.h
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@ extern "C" {
 
 #include "compression_wrapper.h"
 
-#define DEFAULT_DB_COMPRESSION_TYPE             CR_CW_BZ2_COMPRESSION
+#define DEFAULT_DB_COMPRESSION_TYPE             CR_DEFAULT_COMPRESSION
 #define DEFAULT_COMPRESSION_TYPE                CR_DEFAULT_COMPRESSION
 
 typedef enum {
